    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d517">

                <pb facs="0767" n="653" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg653"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">511.4A6/288: Circular telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Certain Diplomatic
                        Representatives in Latin America</hi><anchor n="92" xml:id="d517-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-05-06T16:00:00-04:00">May 6, 1931—4
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Please inform the Government to which you are accredited that this Government has
                    accepted the invitation to participate in the Conference on the Limitation of
                    the Manufacture of Narcotic Drugs which is to convene in Geneva on May 27th;
                    that this Government, as it has stated frequently in the past, believes that the
                    suppression of the illicit traffic in narcotic drugs can be accomplished only by
                    international cooperation of all Governments; and that this Government would be
                    much interested in being informed whether the Government <pb facs="0768" n="654"
                        xml:id="pg654"/> to which you are accredited intends to participate in the
                    Conference referred to. Please reply by telegraph as soon as possible.<anchor
                        n="93" xml:id="d517-f2"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d517-f1" n="92" type="source" xml:id="d517-f1-content">
                <p>The diplomatic missions in Argentina, Bolivia, Brazil, Chile, Colombia, Costa
                    Rica, Dominican Republic, Ecuador, El Salvador, Guatemala, Haiti, Honduras,
                    Nicaragua, Panama, Paraguay, and Peru.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d517-f2" n="93" xml:id="d517-f2-content">
                <p>Telegraphic replies were received in the affirmative from Chile, Costa Rica,
                    Dominican Republic, Ecuador, Argentina, Bolivia, Guatemala, and Paraguay, and in
                    the negative from Colombia, Honduras, Haiti, El Salvador, Panama, and Nicaragua.
                    By mail Peru replied affirmatively and Brazil negatively.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
